.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt LIBWEBPUSH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libwebpush ,
.Nm webpush_encrypt ,
.Nm webpush_vapid ,
.Nm webpush_b64url ,
.Nm webpush_unb64url
.Nd Web Push message encryption and VAPID tokens
.Sh LIBRARY
Web Push Library
.Pq libwebpush , Fl lwebpush Fl lcrypto
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In webpush.h
.Ft int
.Fo webpush_encrypt
.Fa "const uint8_t *ua_pub"
.Fa "const uint8_t *auth"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *as_key"
.Fa "const uint8_t *salt"
.Fa "const uint8_t *plain"
.Fa "size_t plen"
.Fa "uint8_t **outp"
.Fa "size_t *outlenp"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo webpush_vapid
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *key"
.Fa "const char *audience"
.Fa "const char *sub"
.Fa "time_t now"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fn webpush_b64url "const void *data" "size_t len"
.Ft uint8_t *
.Fn webpush_unb64url "const char *s" "size_t *lenp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library does the arithmetic of Web Push: it encrypts a message for one
push subscription, as RFC 8291 has it with the
.Dq aes128gcm
content coding of RFC 8188, and makes the VAPID token of RFC 8292 that
says who sends it.
It speaks no HTTP: the caller posts the result to the subscription's
endpoint with the headers
.Ql Content-Encoding: aes128gcm ,
.Ql TTL
and the
.Ql Authorization
that
.Fn webpush_vapid
returns.
It uses the
.Xr crypto 3
library of OpenSSL.
.Pp
.Fn webpush_encrypt
encrypts the
.Fa plen
bytes at
.Fa plain
for the subscription whose public key
.Pq its Dq p256dh
is the
.Dv WEBPUSH_KEYLEN
(65) bytes of an uncompressed P-256 point at
.Fa ua_pub
and whose authentication secret is the
.Dv WEBPUSH_AUTHLEN
(16) bytes at
.Fa auth .
.Fa as_key
is the sender's P-256 key for this message and
.Fa salt
its
.Dv WEBPUSH_SALTLEN
(16) bytes of salt; when either is
.Dv NULL ,
as it should be outside a test, a new key or random salt is made for
the message.
The message is one record of record size 4096; its body, the header of
RFC 8188 then the record, is returned in
.Pf * Fa outp ,
to be freed with
.Xr free 3 ,
and its length in
.Pf * Fa outlenp .
A message is at most
.Dv WEBPUSH_MAXLEN
(3993) bytes, so that the body is at most the 4096 bytes every push
service takes.
.Pp
.Fn webpush_vapid
returns the value of the
.Ql Authorization
header for a push to the push service at
.Fa audience ,
the origin of the subscription's endpoint
.Pq Dq https://host ,
signed with the application server's P-256
.Fa key :
.Dq vapid t= Ns Ar JWT Ns Dq ", k=" Ns Ar key .
The JWT's
.Dq sub
claim is
.Fa sub ,
a
.Dq mailto:
or
.Dq https:
URI by which the push service may reach the sender, and it expires 12
hours after
.Fa now .
The caller frees the string.
.Pp
.Fn webpush_b64url
returns
.Fa len
bytes of
.Fa data
in base64url without padding, as subscriptions, keys and tokens are
written.
.Fn webpush_unb64url
returns the bytes of the base64url string
.Fa s ,
padded or not, and stores their number in
.Pf * Fa lenp ;
the buffer, which the caller frees, has a byte to spare past them.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn webpush_encrypt
returns 0 on success and \-1 when the message is too long, the
subscription's key is not a P-256 point, or OpenSSL or the memory
fails.
.Fn webpush_vapid ,
.Fn webpush_b64url
and
.Fn webpush_unb64url
return
.Dv NULL
on failure;
.Fn webpush_unb64url
also when
.Fa s
is not base64url, and
.Fn webpush_vapid
when its claims would be longer than 511 bytes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A subscription as the browser's
.Fn PushSubscription.toJSON
gives it, its keys in base64url, encrypted for and signed for:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t *ua, *auth, *body;
size_t len, ualen, authlen;
char *hdr;

ua = webpush_unb64url(p256dh, &ualen);
auth = webpush_unb64url(authsecret, &authlen);
if (ua == NULL || ualen != WEBPUSH_KEYLEN ||
    auth == NULL || authlen != WEBPUSH_AUTHLEN)
	errx(1, "not a subscription");
if (webpush_encrypt(ua, auth, NULL, NULL, msg, strlen(msg),
    &body, &len) != 0)
	errx(1, "webpush_encrypt");
if ((hdr = webpush_vapid(vapid_key, "https://push.example.net",
    "mailto:admin@example.org", time(NULL))) == NULL)
	errx(1, "webpush_vapid");
/* POST body, len bytes, with Authorization: hdr,
 * Content-Encoding: aes128gcm and TTL. */
.Ed
